# The Containerfile copies named paths and never `COPY . .`, so nothing here is
# load-bearing today. It exists so that stays true by accident as well as by
# intent: the image's whole claim is that no build toolchain reaches it, and
# vendor/ is now a real directory in this tree that would contradict that if a
# future COPY were ever written broadly.
vendor/

# Never part of a build context, and both are gitignored besides.
.agents/
.superpowers/
.git/
